savibhattika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (able) to be classified Dhs-a.134. Savupadana = sa-upadana</p><p>sa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->3<!-- raw HTML omitted --> + vibhatti + ka</p>

savicāra|savicaara|savicara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">savicaara</span></p><p>accompanied by investigation DN.i.37 etc., in the description of the first Jhāna. See vicāra.</p>

savidha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective near; (nt.) neighbourhood Dāvs iv.32; Dāvs v.9.</p><p>Sk. savidha</p>

savighāta|savighaata|savighata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">savighaata</span></p><p>adjective bringing vexation Thig.352; Thag-a.242.</p><p>sa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->3<!-- raw HTML omitted --> + vighāta</p>

savijjuka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective accompanied by lightning DN.ii.262.</p><p>sa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->3<!-- raw HTML omitted --> + vijju + ka</p>

savitakka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>accompanied by reasoning DN.i.37 etc., in the formula of the first Jhāna. See vitakka.</p>

saviññāṇa|savi~n~naa.na|savinnana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">savi~n~naa.na</span></p><p>possessed of consciousness, conscious, animate AN.i.83; <em>-<a href="bword://ka">ka</a></em> the same AN.i.132; Dhp-a.i.6<br />■ See <em><a href="bword://vi%C3%B1%C3%B1%C4%81%E1%B9%87aka">viññāṇaka</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ka">ka</a>, <a href="bword://viññāṇaka">viññāṇaka</a></p>

savupādāna|savupaadaana|savupadana
